<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Cananefates</h1><p class="st-meta">50 BCE – 300 CE (approx.) · capital Forum Hadriani</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Germanic people of the Dutch coast near The Hague, kin of the Batavi, who joined the Batavian revolt of 69 CE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> says the Cananefates were related to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/batavi">Batavi</a> and equal to them in origin, language and courage, though fewer in number. They lived in the coastal dunes and peat lands of the western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> mouth and the sea.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/batavi">Batavi</a> they supplied soldiers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, including cavalry units. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> describes how in 69 CE they chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brinno">Brinno</a> as their leader by raising him on a shield, the earliest recorded example of this Germanic custom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brinno">Brinno</a> they attacked Roman forts on the coast at the start of the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-civilis">Julius Civilis</a>. After its defeat they returned to Roman rule, and their chief town became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forum-hadriani">Forum Hadriani</a> (Voorburg), granted market rights under Hadrian. Frankish raids in the 3rd century ended Roman life there.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cananefates.jpg" alt="Cananefates" width="320" height="345"><figcaption>Image: my work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Continental.coast.150AD.Germanic.peoples.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>50 BCE – 300 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Forum Hadriani</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Brinno</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Proto-Germanic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Canninefates</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=125&amp;focus=cananefates" aria-label="Cananefates on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4778 379 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cananefates lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5098 635L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5098 635h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5098 635h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Forum Hadriani. <a href="/atlas?year=125&amp;focus=cananefates">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

